Skepticism was widespread at the time. Apple's sales had dropped 29% the previous year, Gateway had just shuttered 40 of its own stores, and Channel Marketing analyst David Goldstein publicly predicted Apple would be "turning out the lights on a very painful and expensive mistake" within two years.<br/>
<br/>
By 2003, Apple was recording &#36;3 million in profit per store, per quarter, with approximately 60,000 visitors at each location. Apple Retail hit &#36;1.2 billion in revenue in 2004, breaking the record for the fastest retail operation to reach a billion-dollar milestone. The company today operates more than 500 stores across 27 countries, with each location generating approximately &#36;5,500 per square foot annually, among the highest figures in the retail industry.<br/>
<br/>
